    "movableInEdit": false,
    "css": "font-size: 60px;text-align:center",
    "layer": -3,
    "text": "Holders: Layout - pile, singleSpread, & arc"
  },
  "overview": {
    "id": "overview",
    "x": 108,
    "y": 80,
    "width": 1330,
    "height": 150,
    "layer": -3,
    "movable": false,
    "movableInEdit": false,
    "css": "font-size: 25px",
    "html": "This variant covers holders with <b>layout</b> set to &quotpile&quot, &quotsingleSpread&quot, and &quotarc&quot. A single spread has no overflow handling of its own. A hand longer than the holder simply runs past its edge. Arc is the same except the cards will remain inside the holder borders. <b>spreadMin</b> keeps a long fan readable without growing past the right edge for &quotsingleSpread&quot by collapsing all but the specified number of cards. Deal a few cards, then drag them from one holder into the next and watch how each layout receives them"
  },
  "holder1": {
    "type": "holder",
    "id": "holder1",
    "x": 60,
    "y": 250,
    "width": 340,
    "height": 220,
    "onEnter": {
      "activeFace": 1
    }
  },
  "text1": {
    "id": "text1",
    "x": 62,
    "y": 485,
    "width": 340,
    "layer": -3,
    "movable": false,
    "movableInEdit": false,
    "css": {
      "font-size": "22px"
    },
    "html": "No arrangement properties at all: a new holder is on <b>layout</b> &quotauto&quot. Here, that gives a centered row that packs tighter as it fills up."
  },
  "holder2": {
    "type": "holder",
    "id": "holder2",
    "x": 425,
    "y": 250,
    "width": 340,
    "height": 220,
    "onEnter": {
      "activeFace": 1
    },
    "layout": "pile"
  },
  "text2": {
    "id": "text2",
    "x": 427,
    "y": 485,
    "width": 340,
    "layer": -3,
    "movable": false,
    "movableInEdit": false,
    "css": {
      "font-size": "22px"
    },
    "html": "<b>layout</b> &quotpile&quot: one plain stack. Even if the holder is big enough to make spread out arrangements, this layout forces cards into piles. Non-card widgets do not create piles but will be stacked together."
  },
  "holder3": {
